.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt SU 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm su
.Nd become another user
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ss os-real and installed root
.Nm
.Op Fl lmp
.Op Fl s Ar shell
.Op Fl
.Oo Ar user
.Oo Ar file args | Fl c Ar command Op Ar arg0 args
.Oc
.Oc
.Ss os-simple
.Nm
.Op Fl
.Op Fl l | Fl -login
.Op Ar user
.Op Fl c Ar command
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
command runs a shell as another user.
The default user is root.
Both implementations are installed set-user-ID root as
.Pa /bin/su
and authenticate against
.Pa /etc/shadow
unless the caller is root.
.Ss BusyBox su
On os-real and the installed root,
.Nm
is the BusyBox applet from
.Ql busybox-suid .
.Bl -tag -width "-s shell"
.It Fl , Fl l
Run a login shell: the environment is replaced except for
.Ev TERM ,
whatever
.Fl m
or
.Fl p
asked, and the target user's home directory is entered, with a warning
and
.Pa /
instead when it cannot be.
.It Fl m , Fl p
Preserve the environment, except in login mode.
.It Fl s Ar shell
Run the specified shell.
.It Fl c Ar command
Pass the command to the shell with
.Fl c .
.El
.Ss Project su
On os-simple,
.Nm
is the project program.
The options
.Fl ,
.Fl l ,
and
.Fl -login
select login mode.
.Fl c Ar command
runs the target shell as
.Ql "SHELL -c command" .
An unrecognized option or a second user operand is a usage error.
.Pp
A non-root caller is prompted with
.Ql "Password: " ;
the password is read without echo.
An incorrect password or a locked account produces
.Ql "su: authentication failure" .
An unknown user produces
.Ql "su: unknown user NAME" .
The program holds no credential lock.
.Pp
After authentication,
.Nm
closes descriptors 3 through 63, clears supplementary groups,
sets the group ID, and sets the user ID, in that order.
In login mode it then enters the target's home directory;
a failure is fatal.
.Pp
In both modes it builds an environment containing only
.Ev PATH ,
set to
.Ql /bin:/usr/bin ,
and
.Ev HOME ,
.Ev SHELL ,
.Ev USER ,
and
.Ev LOGNAME
from the account record.
It then executes the target's shell.
In login mode,
.Ql argv[0]
is
.Ql -
followed by the shell's base name.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
The project
.Nm
exits with status 1 on authentication, identity, directory, or execution
failure, and 2 on a usage error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Enter the test account's password when prompted:
.Dl su - test -c pwd
The command prints
.Pa /home/test .
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
The project
.Nm
reports:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ql usage: su [-] [-l|--login] [user] [-c command]
Invalid command syntax.
.It Ql su: authentication failure
The password was not accepted or the account is locked.
.It Ql su: unknown user NAME
The account does not exist.
.It Ql su: cannot assume the target identity
Changing the supplementary groups, group ID, or user ID failed.
.It Ql su: cannot enter DIR
The home directory could not be entered in login mode.
.It Ql su: cannot exec SHELL
The target shell could not be executed.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr login 1 ,
.Xr passwd 1 ,
.Xr shadow 5
